        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-24 04:30:45.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nNeeds a refresh: the file named in the quoted build error is not converted, so the in-kernel build still fails (see the /COMMIT_MSG comment). Separately, around 19 other files still include headers by their lustre_compat/linux/... path (folio.h, shrinker.h, uio.h, timer.h, rbtree.h, mm.h, string.h, ...), e.g. lustre/obdclass/lu_object.c and lustre/osc/osc_request.c. If copy-builtin really drops include/lustre_compat, won't those break the in-kernel build the same way? If they are fine for some reason, saying why in the commit message would help; otherwise this might be better done as one sweep.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
