          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 16:30:47.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21099 build: include workqueue.h by its kernel path",
        "message": "LU-21099 build: include workqueue.h by its kernel path\n\nThe in-kernel build of Lustre fails with:\n\n  fs/lustre/obdclass/hash.c:87:10: fatal error:\n  'lustre_compat/linux/workqueue.h' file not found\n\ncopy-builtin leaves include/lustre_compat behind, since it only\nbackfills newer kernel APIs on older kernels.  The headers there\nshadow the kernel ones through the include path, so the callers\nmust name the kernel header and not the compat directory.\n\nInclude <linux/workqueue.h> in the four files that took WQ_PERCPU\nfrom the compat path.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 8740186a76a9 (\"LU-21099 build: pass WQ_PERCPU to per-CPU workqueues\")\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I98573ce041a565f05a78964ac304eb0f6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
